    <h2>🎯 Who doneche Is For</h2>
    <p>doneche is built for anyone actively applying to jobs who wants clarity instead of chaos. That includes:</p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Active job seekers</strong> juggling 10+ open applications at once and losing track of status.</li>
      <li><strong>Fresh graduates</strong> entering the job market for the first time, who need a simple system (and templates) to stay organized and professional.</li>
      <li><strong>Career switchers</strong> applying across multiple domains/roles who need to track very different pipelines simultaneously.</li>
      <li><strong>Passive job seekers</strong> quietly exploring a few select opportunities while employed, who want a lightweight way to track without a spreadsheet.</li>
      <li><strong>Anyone who's been "ghosted" before</strong> and wants a system that removes the guesswork of when to follow up.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Who doneche is NOT for</h3>
    <p>doneche isn't a recruiting tool for HR teams or hiring managers — it's built exclusively for the applicant's side of the process.</p>

    <p>Curious if doneche fits your search? <a href="/register">Try it free</a> or read <a href="/best-practices">the best way to use doneche</a>.</p>
  </main>

